    "raw": "Given: Maria received a 25% discount, which amounted to $40.\n\nTo find: The total amount Maria paid after the discount.\n\nFirst, let's identify the original price before the discount. Since 25% of the original price is $40, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 0.25 \\times \\text{Original Price} = 40 \\]\n\nSolving for the original price:\n\n\\[ \\text{Original Price} = \\frac{40}{0.25} = 160 \\]\n\nSo, the original price of the DVDs was $160.\n\nNext, we need to find out how much Maria paid after the discount. The discount amount is $40, so we subtract this from the original price:\n\n\\[ \\text{Amount Paid} = \\text{Original Price} - \\text{Discount} = 160 - 40 = 120 \\]\n\nTherefore, Maria paid a total of $120.\n\nFINAL: 120",
